object:
  title: "Layer 2 fees drop 90-99%; a $5 mainnet swap costs $0.05 on Arbitrum"
  type: claim-evidence
  claim: >-
    "Fees drop 90-99%. A $5 swap on mainnet might cost $0.05 on Arbitrum."
  evidence: >-
    Presented as a general rule with one illustrative example; no specific
    date, transaction, or data source is cited in the article.
  source_lineage: src/content/docs/gas-fees.md (no external source cited)
  interpretation: >-
    Directionally consistent with well-known Layer 2 cost advantages (L2s
    batch transactions off mainnet, sharing settlement costs); the specific
    "$5 → $0.05" figure is illustrative, not a live quote.
  uncertainty: >-
    Both mainnet and L2 gas costs fluctuate constantly with network demand;
    the 90-99% range and the $5/$0.05 example are approximations that will
    drift and should not be quoted as current pricing without re-checking
    live gas trackers.
